ent & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 418 people. Revenue per employee of $364K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $21K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["SmartRent, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $302M market cap on $152M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -47% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $25M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -12.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -315.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 49% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 196% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SmartRent (NYSE:SMRT) Issues Earnings Results, Meets Expectations","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/smartrent-nysesmrt-issues-earnings-results-meets-expectations.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793844649.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","legal"]},{"title":"SmartRent Inc (SMRT) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Margins, Surging Bookings and a ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/smartrent-inc-smrt-q3-2026-011253639.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793841173.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"SmartRent (SMRT) Q3 2026 Earnings Call T